DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSF State’s Free Public Rooft
 op Stargazing Nights w/ Huge Telescope (Fall 2026)San Francisco State Univ
 ersity Observatory hosts a free public open night with family-friendly ast
 ronomy talks\, updates on astronomy research\, and rooftop telescope obser
 ving. Programming is offered in English and Spanish\, weather permitting.\
 nLocated at SFSU Thornton Hall top floor\n\nUpcoming Weekly Schedule Throu
 gh Dec. 4\, 2026\nWednesday\, Thursday + Friday evenings when skies are cl
 ear.\n– September: 7:30-9:30 PM.\n– October: 7:00-9:30 PM.\n– Novemb
 er/December*: 6:30-9:00 PM (thru 12/4)\nNovember/December 2026 Closures\n\
 nThe observatory will be CLOSED for Veterans day\, Wednesday\, Nov 11.\nTh
 e observatory will be CLOSED during Fall Recess\, November 23-27\, 2026.\n
 The Observatory will be CLOSED the last week of classes (Dec 7-11).\n\nThe
  LAST open public night (weather permitting) will be Friday\, Dec 4\, 2026
 \n*** The Observatory is open ONLY when skies are clear! Please see SF Sta
 te Instagram to check if we are closed due to poor weather conditions! ***
 \nThe SF State Observatory is a student-run facility open to all students\
 , staff\, and members of the public two or three nights per week in fall a
 nd spring semesters. With the aid of observatory docents\, visitors use te
 lescopes to look at craters on the Moon\, planets\, beautiful binary stars
 \, star clusters\, nebulae\, and more. SF State students: need a study bre
 ak? Drop by\, and bring a friend!\nThornton Hall\, 10th Floor\nSan Francis
 co St...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.instagram.com/p/DdnGZdLNdTy/?utm_
 source=ig_web_copy_link&amp\;stkn=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ==\nDetails: https://sf.fu
 ncheap.com/sf-states-free-public-rooftop-stargazing-nights-w-huge-telescop
 e-october-2026-7/\nSource: Funcheap SF
