DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSan Francisco Bike Party hosts
  a goth-themed Bats vs. Cats group ride along the city’s eastern waterfr
 ont. Meet at the William McKinley Statue in the Panhandle at 7:30 PM for a
 n 8 PM rollout\, with stops at Warm Water Cove Park and Exploratorium Pier
  15 before ending at Mission Creek Park North. Decorative bat wings and ca
 t ears will be offered for a suggested $5 donation benefiting the San Fran
 cisco SPCA and NorCal Bats.\nKick off spooky season with our goth themed C
 ats vs Bats ride this Friday October 2nd! Join us for a super chill ride a
 long San Francisco’s eastern waterfront. Expect equal parts riding and p
 artying 🪩🚲\n\nDecorative bat wings and cat ears will be available fo
 r a suggested $5 donation. ALL proceeds will go to @sanfranciscospca and @
 norcalbats. Stop by the bikecurious bike to get your pair.\nPoster designe
 d by Valentine\nLook books by @bikepretty\nTheme: Bats vs. Cats\nStart: Wi
 lliam McKinley Statue in the Panhandle\nStop 1: Warm Water Cover Park\nSto
 p 2: Exploratorium Pier 15\nEnd: Mission Creek Park North\nRoute Map:\nhtt
 ps://maps.app.goo.gl/QaF3JPSvp2tQZY5JA\nMeetup: 7:30 pm PST\nRollout: 8 pm
  PST\nHow We Ride:\n• Stay in the RIGHT lane\n• Stop at RED lights\n
 • Leave no trace\n• Ride predictably & in control\n• Roll past confl
 ict\n• Ride prepared\n• When in doubt\, BIKE PARTY!\n@bikecuriouslive\
 nBikeCurious\nCar free living in San Francisco\, CA. Live on Twitch every 
 Sunday at 1pm PST 👇\ntwitch.tv/bikecurious\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://
 www.instagram.com/p/Dd2oFZxlDu_/?utm_source=ig_web_copy_link&amp\;stkn=NTc
 4MTIwNjQ2YQ==\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/sf-bike-partys-bats-cats-g
 oth-bike-ride-2026-gg-park-waterfront/\nSource: Funcheap SF
