DESCRIPTION:“Beyond Walls” Join 1000-Person Human Chain Around Huge Ar
 twork (Yerba Buena Gardens)\nSaype’s Beyond Walls in Minneapolis. A new 
 installation is coming to Yerba Buena Gardens\nA massive\, ephemeral artwo
 rk by world-renowned artist Saype\, will be painted across San Francisco
 ’s Yerba Buena Gardens’ Great Lawn.\nBeyond Walls depicts giant intert
 wined hands painted on the ground symbolizing the longest human chain in t
 he world\, step-by-step\, city-by-city — a global effort to promote toge
 therness\, kindness and openness. This temporary\, biodegradable fresco is
  an invitation to pause\, to look\, and to remember that we are linked.\n\
 nBeyond Walls Schedule at Yerba Buena Gardens\n\nMonday-Wednesday\, Octobe
 r 5-7\, Live Painting by Saype at Yerba Buena Gardens\nWednesday\, October
  7\, 4:30PM: Public Celebration\, Human Chain with Nearly 1\,000 Locking H
 ands Around the Artwork\nFriday\, October 9: Artist Talk with Saype at YBC
 A\n\nGreat Lawn\, Yerba Buena Gardens\, Mission St. between 3rd and 4th St
 s.\, SF\nFREE\nCome together and join hands!\nOn October 7\, be part of ar
 t history! Gather in community and join hands around the artwork for an un
 forgettable photo moment. RSVP\n\nUpcoming “Beyond Walls” Join 1000-Pe
 rson Human Chain Around Huge Artwork (Yerba Buena Gardens) Events\nMon 10/
 5 Watch Huge “Beyond Walls” Grass Mural Being Painted on SF’s Yerba 
 Buena Gardens (Oct. 5-7)Tue 10/6 Watch Huge “Beyond Walls” Grass Mural
  Being Painted on SF’s Yerba Buena Gardens (Oct. 5-7)Wed 10/7 “Beyond 
 Walls” Join 1000-Person Hu...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite
 .com/e/beyond-walls-be-part-of-a-massive-artwork-tickets-2001093019088\nDe
 tails: https://sf.funcheap.com/watch-huge-beyond-walls-grass-mural-being-p
 ainted-on-sfs-yerba-buena-gardens-oct-5-7/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/image-
 4-e1790027445466.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Great Lawn\, Yerba Buena Gardens\, Mission St. between 3rd & 4th 
 Sts. San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
