DESCRIPTION:BORP Adaptive Sports and RecreationSan Francisco shines in Oct
 ober! Let’s spend some time outside together and explore Golden Gate Par
 k on wheels. San Francisco Village\, BORP Adaptive Sports and Recreation\,
  and the San Francisco Bicycle Coalition are partnering to bring together 
 riders of all ages and will have bikes to available to meet your accessibi
 lity needs. This ride is perfect for elders\, families with kids\, and any
 one who would like to enjoy the park on a beautiful Friday afternoon.\nLet
  us know what would help you join us – BORP will provide recumbent elect
 ric assist bikes\, tandem side by side bikes\, bikes with recumbent seats\
 , and more! If you have a body\, we’ll do our best to find a bike with t
 he right fit/support. If you are borrowing an accessible bike\, plan to ge
 t to the Bandshell by 2:00 PM to sign a waiver and find the right fit. If 
 you want to partner with someone to help them ride\, let us know and come 
 by 2:00 PM.\nYou are also welcome to bring and ride your own bike! The pac
 e will be slow and conversational and we don’t drop anyone. The route ca
 n be found at https://ridewithgps.com/routes/56763052. Organizers request 
 you wear a helmet as well\; BORP will have some available for those using 
 an accessible bike.\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://sfbike.org/event/intergene
 rational-and-accessible-bike-ride-in-golden-gate-park/\nDetails: https://s
 f.funcheap.com/slowpaced-golden-gate-park-ride-adaptive-bikes-sf/\nSource:
