BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The 5th Annual Berkeley Bird Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T170000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1639081@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Nature
DESCRIPTION:Golden Gate Bird AllianceThe Berkeley Bird Festival\nSunday\, 
 October 18th\nberkeleybirdfestival.org\nThe David Brower Center | 2150 All
 ston Way\, Berkeley (12-5pm)\nBirding Field Trips | Various Parks Around B
 erkeley (8am-5pm)\n\nFree | Family-Friendly | All Ages\nEvery bird holds a
  memory. Every memory holds a meaning. Across different cultures and commu
 nities\, across time and space\, birds have played a significant role in s
 haping our understanding of the world\, ourselves\, and our relationship i
 n nature.\nOn Sunday\, October 18th\, this year’s Berkeley Bird Festival
  invites you to celebrate our incredible birdlife here in the Bay Area thr
 ough the theme of “Myth and Memories”.\nGet outside and witness the bi
 rds and our shared environment. Engage with the Myth of the Flying African
 s. Fold a crane for peace and longevity. Hear the story of SF’s Wild Par
 rots. Watch the street “split the sky” through a dance inspired by mig
 ration. Listen to the science behind wildlife and remember\, every feather
 \, past and present\, is a portal to a world where all of us thrive.\nThis
  festival brings science\, art\, and culture under its wing to inspire our
  collective imagination and action in protecting birds and our environment
 . We hope you’ll join us whether you’re bird-curious or a long-time ad
 vocate.\nRegister in advance to attend a trip\, or gather your flock\, swo
 op in\, and dive into a world of birds\, Myth and Memory.\n#MythandMemory 
 #BerkeleyBirdFest2026 #BBF2026\nTransportation: We highly recommend taking
  pub...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.berkeleybirdfestival.org\nDetails:
  https://sf.funcheap.com/5th-annual-berkeley-bird-festival/\nSource: Funch
 eap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Design
 -1-8.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
