BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:City Creatures: Pest Art Pop-Up
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261030T230000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1637042@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Nature
DESCRIPTION:Pestec\n​Art. Urban wildlife. Guest speakers. Food. Drinks. 
 Music. And a gallery full of strange things to explore.\n\nCity Creatures 
 is a one-day exhibition at Terra Gallery exploring the hidden ecology of c
 ity life through art\, science\, and the perspective of people who work cl
 osely with urban systems.\nThe event brings together artists\, scientists\
 , environmental professionals\, and Pestec’s field perspective on pests\
 , wildlife\, waste\, buildings\, and infrastructure.\nThe free daytime ope
 n house includes installations\, talks\, and interactive work. The evening
  continues with music and a fundraiser benefiting USF’s Gellert Family B
 usiness Center.\n\nCity Creatures: Pest Art Pop-Up\nFriday\, October 30\, 
 2026 | 2p – 11p\nTerra Gallery\, 511 Harrison St\, SF – maps\nFree –
  RSVP | Open House Daytime Exhibit\nGet Tickets – $15 | Night Party + Fu
 ndraiser\nSchedule:\n\n2pm-6pm: free to the public\, educational craft fai
 r with speakers\, art\, vendors\, and music\n6pm-11pm: ticketed fundraiser
  & halloween party with art\, vendors\, live music\, food and drinks\n\n
 ​all evening ticket proceeds support the University of San Francisco Gel
 lert Family Business Center’s Next Gen Business Initiative.\nView the Fu
 ll Program\nStreet parking is available after 5pm\, with a garage located 
 across the street. Public transit is also convenient\, with a 10-minute wa
 lk from Montgomery Station. Kids are welcome\, and costumes are encouraged
 !\nUrban Reflections\nWhen you see a pest\, what do we see? Many people se
 e something dirty or unke...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://citycreatures.my.
 canva.site/city-creatures/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/city-creature
