DESCRIPTION:SF State’s Free Public Rooftop Stargazing Nights w/ Huge Tel
 escope (Fall 2026)\nSan Francisco State University Observatory\nSan Franci
 sco State University Observatory hosts a free public open night with famil
 y-friendly astronomy talks\, updates on astronomy research\, and rooftop t
 elescope observing. Programming is offered in English and Spanish\, weathe
 r permitting.\nLocated at SFSU Thornton Hall top floor\nUpcoming Weekly Sc
 hedule Through Dec. 4\, 2026\nWednesday\, Thursday + Friday evenings when 
 skies are clear.\n– September: 7:30-9:30 PM.\n– October: 7:00-9:30 PM.
 \n– November/December*: 6:30-9:00 PM (thru 12/4)\n\nNovember/December 20
 26 Closures\n\nThe observatory will be CLOSED for Veterans day\, Wednesday
 \, Nov 11.\nThe observatory will be CLOSED during Fall Recess\, November 2
 3-27\, 2026.\nThe Observatory will be CLOSED the last week of classes (Dec
  7-11).\n\nThe LAST open public night (weather permitting) will be Friday\
 , Dec 4\, 2026\n*** The Observatory is open ONLY when skies are clear! Ple
 ase see SF State Instagram to check if we are closed due to poor weather c
 onditions! ***\nThe SF State Observatory is a student-run facility open to
  all students\, staff\, and members of the public two or three nights per 
 week in fall and spring semesters. With the aid of observatory docents\, v
 isitors use telescopes to look at craters on the Moon\, planets\, beautifu
 l binary stars\, star clusters\, nebulae\, and more. SF State students: ne
 ed a study break? Drop by\, and bring a friend!\nThornton Hall\, 10th Floo
 r\nSan...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.instagram.com/p/DdnGZdLNdTy/?utm
